<%# ── Workflows ── %>
<section class="guide__section" id="workflows">
  <h2 class="guide__section-heading">Workflows</h2>

  <div class="guide__workflow-grid">
    <div class="guide__workflow">
      <div class="guide__workflow-icon">
        <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <path d="M17 3a2.85 2.85 0 1 1 4 4L7.5 20.5 2 22l1.5-5.5Z"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <h3 class="guide__workflow-title">Agent Feedback Loop</h3>
      <p class="guide__workflow-desc">The agent screenshots its own work, you review and annotate, it reads your feedback and iterates. Each iteration is saved as a new version under the same page.</p>
      <ol class="guide__workflow-steps">
        <li>Type <code>/screenote &lt;url&gt;</code> &mdash; agent captures the page</li>
        <li>Open the screenshot and mark what's wrong</li>
        <li>Type <code>/screenote feedback</code> &mdash; agent reads your annotations with the cropped images</li>
        <li>Agent fixes the issues, re-screenshots to the same page, and repeats</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="guide__workflow">
      <div class="guide__workflow-icon">
        <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <path d="M21 15a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H7l-4 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"/>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <h3 class="guide__workflow-title">Capture &amp; Annotate</h3>
      <p class="guide__workflow-desc">You upload a screenshot, mark what's wrong, and your AI agent picks up the feedback.</p>
      <ol class="guide__workflow-steps">
        <li>Upload a screenshot in the Screenote UI</li>
        <li>Draw rectangles around problems and write comments</li>
        <li>Your agent reads the annotations with the cropped image</li>
        <li>Agent fixes the issue and marks it resolved</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# ── How It's Organized ── %>
  <div class="guide__concepts">
    <h3 class="guide__concepts-title">How screenshots are organized</h3>
    <p class="guide__concepts-desc">Screenote uses a three-level hierarchy to keep your feedback organized:</p>
    <div class="guide__concepts-list">
      <div class="guide__concept">
        <strong>Project</strong> &mdash; your app or product (e.g., &ldquo;Screenote&rdquo;)
      </div>
      <div class="guide__concept">
        <strong>Page</strong> &mdash; a screen or view you're iterating on (e.g., &ldquo;Login&rdquo;, &ldquo;Dashboard&rdquo;)
      </div>
      <div class="guide__concept">
        <strong>Version</strong> &mdash; each screenshot upload, so you can track iterations over time
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="guide__concepts-desc">When an agent uploads a screenshot, it's automatically grouped under a page. Multiple uploads to the same page become versions, giving you a visual history of changes.</p>
  </div>
</section>
